{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791235694,"nonce":"ePLcj/g13aR3gDk4bkRRBwSW03o=","title":"Use text-measure baselines instead of the post-layout baseline pass","message":"taffy 0.14 lets a measure function return a full LayoutOutput, including baselines. The text measure function in tree.rs wraps compute_leaf_layout, which returns Baselines::NONE, so align-items: baseline still falls back to box bottoms and LayoutTree::align_baselines corrects it afterwards with a side table of shifts applied in get_bounds/get_absolute_bounds.\n\nReturning the text leaf's real first baseline from the measure function could let taffy's flexbox align it directly and retire the post-pass, its wrapped-line grouping, and the out-of-flow exclusions. Needs the baseline from the font metrics at measure time (ascender plus half-leading, as drawn_baseline in tests/baseline_alignment.rs computes it) and must keep that file's cases passing, including wrapped rows and mixed families.","files":null}]}